{"chunk_id": "6b73419c8039", "text": "Damayanti, separated from Nala and reduced to wandering in misery, reaches the city of the Chedi king Suvahu wearing only half a garment. Frightened, exhausted, and surrounded by curious townspeople, she is noticed by the compassionate queen\u2011mother, who senses nobility beneath her distress. Questioned by the nurse, Damayanti recounts her loyalty to her husband Nala, his ruin at dice, and how he abandoned her in the forest after cutting away half her cloth. The queen offers refuge, and Damayanti accepts under strict vows protecting her dignity and fidelity. Meanwhile, the narrative shifts to Nala in the forest, where he rescues the cursed serpent Karkotaka from a wildfire. The serpent bites him deliberately, transforming his appearance to hide him and promising protection while the spirit that ruined him suffers within.\nDamayanti, destitute, finds refuge with the Chedi queen under strict vows while Nala rescues the cursed serpent Karkotaka and is transformed by its bite.\nThemes: exile and loyalty, hidden identity, divine curse and fate, hospitality and protection", "vector": [0.019732153043150902, -0.016650283709168434, -0.004783035721629858, -0.027286827564239502, -0.020795809105038643, 0.028527757152915, -0.019963975995779037, -0.013677505776286125, -0.01545026246458292, -0.021150359883904457, 0.02563679963350296, 0.018886685371398926, 0.017754847183823586, 0.01692301593720913, -0.0007547003333456814, 0.0046705338172614574, 0.04655533656477928, -0.013097950257360935, 0.01341159176081419, -0.020523076876997948, -0.0022739022970199585, 0.012832036241889, 0.005284180864691734, 0.020536713302135468, -0.017809394747018814, 0.002381290541961789, 0.025923168286681175, -0.028909582644701004, 0.008502417244017124, -0.022882208228111267, -0.009150155819952488, -0.0033477842807769775, 0.00017791496065910906, -0.028145933523774147, -0.03259146213531494, 0.0021034448873251677, 9.359179239254445e-05, -0.013275225646793842, 0.011829746